    "title": "Tallahassee sandwich shop Which Wich location closed for good, one still remains - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kyla A Sanford ,\n8 hours ago After 10 years of operation the fast casual sandwich shop Which Wich Superior Sandwiches is closed for good.\nIn case you're still wondering which one we're referring to, it's the shop located on Magnolia Drive, between Park Avenue and Governors Square Boulevard in the Magnolia Grove shopping center.\nIt was the third shop to open in the capital city on Sept. 23, 2015 in a series of back-to-back expansions as the local stores helped put the Texas brand on the map when it came to exceeding in sales.\nA note posted on the doors of the vibrant yellow building and Google listing marked \"Permanently closed\" signal the end of the location's demise.\n\"After reaching the end of our lease, we have decided to close this location,\" the note said. \"We are grateful for ten fantastic years and grateful to every customer and all the relationships we have built over the years.\"\nThis is the second Which Wich location to close this year as the storefront in The Village Commons shopping center shuttered in January.\nThe sandwich shop is known for its variety of “wiches,\" customized for every taste. One of the more popular items is the Wicked — it’s piled with five meats (turkey, ham, roast beef, pepperoni and bacon), topped with up to three different cheeses.\nNo worries, one location on 3020 W. Pensacola St. still remains. It sits next door to sweet shop, More Than Pudding.\nThis article includes previously reported information.\nKyla A Sanford covers dining and entertainment for the Tallahassee Democrat. New restaurant opening up, special deals, or events coming up? Let me know at ksanford@tallahassee.com. You can also email your suggestions for a future TLH Eats restaurant profile.\nThis article originally appeared on Tallahassee Democrat: Tallahassee sandwich shop Which Wich location closed for good, one still remains\n2",
